    "turn_text": "good good summary bill that's uh... what what the legislature did that are are urging, and we implemented it this past week with an executive order. One of the things I've been interested in for many, many years is the problems we're having in regard to foster care and adoption. And you and I talked about this before, but we have too many children who just languish in foster care, and they're never adopted You know, and they basically age out they get to be 17 18 years of age and they've never never been adopted so Having children adopted having them in stable homes is so very very important yet. We know that You know, some families simply cannot afford to do that. And, you know, you noted, especially the money for adopting a child who has special needs, you know, those children do incur additional costs. And a lot of people would love to do that, but they simply, you know, do not have the resources to do that. So this is something that, you know, we think is going to make a big difference. It's going to help. It's going to get more kids adopted. And it's really, really very, very important.",
