    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Well, I'm not sure that's really true, Bill. I know that a lot of people want to say that. Abortion is a very contentious issue. It is something that people feel very strongly about on both sides. And you do have people who are pro-life, who will tell you they're pro-life. And then if you get a further discussion and you talk about someone who is raped or incest, and then they'll back off a little bit and they'll say, well, I think there should be exception there. Now, look, I'm pro-life, I think we're dealing with a human being, I think we're dealing with a child, whatever the cause, however that happened. And of course, great, great, great tragedy. But I do think that what we're facing within Ohio now is an effort by the really pro-abortion people to take this issue to the ballot in the fall and try to engrave in the Ohio Constitution an Ohio constitutional right to abortion. And I think that would be you know it's the wrong thing to do i am adamantly opposed to that uh... you know if that passes in the fall we become california we become new york which is basically with virtually no limitations uh... on on abortion and the american people and certainly the people all high up to stay with the people who are people are certainly not in favor of that so uh... what i've advise the legislature and they, you know, they, we have equal branches of government so they can do what, you know, what they think is best. But I've simply said, as we look at, you know, the law in regard to abortion, we have a heartbeat bill that the courts have blocked, but I think they will, you know, at some point that's going to open back up and the heartbeat bill will actually become law in the state of Ohio, sorry, law will become an effect in the state of Ohio. But I think that the vast majority of people will, or certainly for that, but if you added a exception for rape and incest, then I think that will What is most people will say, yes, I agree with that. My concern is what happens in the fall, and people say, well, gee, I think there should be an exception, or I think this, and they go ahead and vote for this, what I consider to be a radical constitutional amendment, where they want, it's not just a law, they want to engrave this in the Ohio Constitution. That's kind of how I look at this thing from a pro-life point of view and trying to save lives. Let's make sure that what we have on the books is something that the vast majority of Ohioans find acceptable. And I think if we do that, then we'll be able to defeat the effort to have this very, very liberal, very, very I think wrong constitutional member.",
