  {
    "episode_id": 81498,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "Bill, I don't know if I would push from that, but I think that You know, what our goal has been and what I have said consistently from day one is that the railroad caused this problem. You know, it's their train, it's their track, it's their rack. And but for the railroad, people would be, you know, going about their business. And so the railroad has an obligation to make the community whole and make individuals whole. So if someone sells their house, can't sell their house, let's say a house was worth 100,000 and now the house sells for 50,000. I believe the railroad owes that person $50,000. That's how I would approach it.",
