  {
    "episode_id": 81498,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "Yes, look, I mean, look, people have a right as much as humanly possible to be put back in the position they were five minutes before the train wreck. And I will say this. We had some problems with the railroad in communication within the first day or so. But when we've requested them to pay for something, or the fire chief has asked them to do something, or the chief, or the mayor, so far, they've been willing to do that. So I think what we end up, Bill, to make sure that this is taken care of in the long run, what we end up with is a fund that will have to be funded by the railroad. As you know, there's a lot of lawsuits, class action lawsuits, so eventually a court will take jurisdiction over this. But I told the railroad that the sooner they can establish a fund, I think the better people will feel that there are real dollars there. And then when the courts get around to it, and I don't know how long that will be, but when it works its way through the courts, the courts can bless that and take supervision over that.",
